# Architecture

Layout for this stack: **React + Vite** SPA (`frontend/`), **FastAPI** (`backend/`), **Supabase** (Auth + Postgres **app schema**, lowercase product name). No microservices, GraphQL, or custom frameworks unless explicitly approved.

## Monorepo layout

```
<repo>/
├── frontend/                 # Vite React SPA
├── backend/                  # FastAPI (Python 3.12)
├── supabase/migrations/      # sole source of DB truth
├── vercel.json               # frontend deploy when Vercel root = repo root
├── package.json              # Husky + eslint → frontend lint
└── README.md
```

Do not introduce `apps/web`, `apps/api`, or `packages/shared` in this repo. Layout is `frontend/` + `backend/` + `supabase/`.

## System boundaries

```text
Browser
  ├─ Supabase Auth SDK     → login, session, token refresh only
  └─ HTTPS + Bearer JWT    → all business reads/writes

API (service_role)         → Postgres (app schema), RPC, R2, Stripe
Postgres (app schema)      → system of record
R2                         → catalog image bytes; object key in DB; serve via API proxy
```

**Hard rules**

- Frontend **never** uses service_role or reads business tables via anon key.
- Frontend **never** sets catalog prices on write — server resolves from `catalog_products`. Exception: **venta libre** (`libre-varios`) may send `unitPrice`.
- One catalog source of truth in Postgres (not static TS product arrays).
- Schema changes only via `supabase/migrations/` — never “just run SQL in dashboard” without committing a migration file.

## Layer model (API)

```text
server.py          FastAPI app, CORS, mount /api
api/router.py      /health, /me, include domain routers
api/*_routes.py    HTTP adapter + mapping (Pydantic in, camelCase out)
api/deps.py        require_pos_staff, require_admin
api/*.py           helpers (config, r2, fulfillment, checkout guards)
```

There is **no** `services/` / `repositories/` split. Keep logic in the domain route module or a sibling helper (`shop_fulfillment.py`, `shop_checkout_guards.py`) when the file is already large. Do not add a Node/Fastify layer.

## Layer model (web)

```text
App.tsx            providers + routes
pages/             route views
components/        shared + POS UI
context/           Auth, Cart, Catalog, Pos
lib/               apiClient, supabase (auth only), domain *Api.ts
```

No `features/` folders, no `@/` path alias, no TanStack Query. Server data: `fetch` in `lib/*Api.ts` + React context / local state.

## Deploy model

- **Two Vercel projects**: frontend (repo root `vercel.json` → `frontend/dist`) and backend (root `backend/`).
- Build-time env (`VITE_*`) on web — this repo uses **`VITE_BACKEND_URL`**, not `VITE_API_URL`.
- Runtime env on API (`SUPABASE_*`, `R2_*`, `STRIPE_*`).

## State ownership

| Concern | Owner |
|---------|--------|
| Session / JWT | Supabase Auth (client) |
| Role / permissions | API `GET /api/me` — not PostgREST from browser |
| Catalog / cart | `CatalogContext`, `CartContext` |
| POS ticket | `PosContext` |
| UI ephemeral | `useState` |

No Redux/Zustand/TanStack Query.

## What we deliberately skip

Microservices, GraphQL, event sourcing, Kubernetes, SSR/Next, BFF, CQRS, `packages/shared` Zod, Node API rewrite.

## Anti-patterns

- ❌ Business data fetched with anon key from browser
- ❌ Client-sent `unitPrice` trusted for catalog products (venta libre only)
- ❌ Multiple SQL schema files contradicting runtime (`backend/supabase_schema.sql` vs `supabase/migrations/`)
- ❌ Pretending the API is Node/Fastify or the web lives under `apps/web`
